"""The Cognito token check and the role check.

A slice adds `require_roles` to each operation that is not public:

    @router.get("/orders", dependencies=[Depends(require_roles("clerk", "admin"))])

The check returns HTTP 401 if the request has no valid access token. It
returns HTTP 403 if no group in the claim `cognito:groups` is in the
permitted roles. An operation with `public = true` does not use the check,
and thus needs no token.

The check reads the user pool values from the configuration at run time.
It keeps the JWKS of the user pool in memory, and gets it again only when
a token has an unknown key ID.
"""

